        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented the INI parser in MoonBit for `specs/ini.md`, as a real line-oriented parser (no fixture special-casing), organized by pipeline stage in the package root.\n\n## What was built\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `char_class.mbt` (42 L) | The dialect's character classes: blanks (` `/`\\t`), comment markers (`;`/`#`), quotes, control characters — one definition each, shared by parser and printer |\n| `scanner.mbt` (88 L) | Physical lines: LF/CRLF splitting (a CR not part of CRLF stays content), slicing, blank trimming |\n| `value.mbt` (215 L) | Value carriers, per-carrier escape decoding, inline-comment stripping, `\\` continuation joining, quoted values |\n| `parser.mbt` (185 L) | Line classification, section headers (trimmed names, whole-name quote unwrapping, nested-bracket/empty/trailing-text rejection, re-open), keys (first `=`/`:` wins, control-char rejection), entry insertion into global/current section |\n| `printer.mbt` (89 L) | `print`: values always double-quoted with 4 escapes, section names bare unless the parser would alter them, sorted deterministic output |\n| `errors.mbt` (14 L) | `fail_at` — the single place that formats `ini: line N: …` |\n\nKey ordering decisions (documented in code and README): continuation is decided on the raw line before escapes (odd/even backslash-run table), an inline comment needs a preceding blank and applies only to the entry's own line (continuation text is data, per the spec's \"contributes text, not syntax\"), then trimming, then escape decoding.\n\n## Validation actually run\n\n- `moon check` → 0 errors, 0 warnings (the only two diagnostics suppressed in `moon.pkg` are the ones the immutable provided files raise: `deprecated_syntax` from `ini_spec.mbt`, `test_unqualified_package` from `ini_pub_test.mbt` — verified by enabling them and observing exactly those two).\n- `moon test` → **50/50 pass**: the 12 provided tests (incl. both QuickCheck properties), 33 spec-derived rule tests (`ini_extra_test.mbt`), and 5 properties (`ini_property_test.mbt`: hostile round-trips, idempotent printing, 2000-case no-panic fuzz).\n- `moon fmt` over the implementation files (my files are format-clean); `moon info` regenerates `pkg.generated.mbti` unchanged.\n- `ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, and `specs/` are byte-for-byte back to their original content (line counts 94/151/145) — an earlier `moon fmt` run had rewritten two of them, which I detected via an audit and restored.\n- An independent audit (`@builtin/review.mbtx`) reviewed the code against the spec with ~105 extra hand-built inputs and found 4 findings (0 blockers); all were addressed: the continuation/inline-comment ordering now follows the spec sentence, stray non-CRLF `\\r` is preserved, the warning-suppression justification is accurate again, and the README numbers were corrected.\n\n## Remaining judgment calls (spec leaves them open)\n\n- `print` always emits double-quoted values (`key=\"value\"`), since the spec says the text is unspecified and describes double quotes as the carrier for any value.\n- A repeated section header re-opens the map (last-wins on duplicate keys), and `[]`/`[\"\"]` are rejected as empty names."
        }
